 {"evidence_run_id": "a9b1feeb", "status": "complete", "id": "AUG-150", "title": "Obligation gate is still bypassable: a verification block with method=\"test\" and a path but no type=\"test\" is never checked", "detail": {"fingerprint": "0407d2ec118088b39b8846b8c9cf2361065fd3758650f5261cfe30725282e865", "evidence": [{"run_id":"a9b1feeb","ts":"2026-11-11T02:02:35.42686+00:00","tree_fp":"fdb2c8b3dbb3ca62a4f7764e24ad5fb340b94c800f77db1cddacc305f4a8442f","artifacts":[".gitreins/history/2026-11-11/a9b1feeb/verdict.json"]}]}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05 on the merged wave tree (2815262 + corpus). Reproduce: take the shipped specs/verification.xml and change one verification block's path to tests/does-not-exist.py, leaving method=\"test\" runner=\"pytest\" selector=... intact -> `auger spec check specs` returns {\"status\": \"valid\"} and `auger spec validate specs` rc 0. Add type=\"test\" to the same block -> the same corpus is refused: 'stale-test-ref: verification.xml: SPEC-OBL-CONSUMER-V1: tests/does-not-exist.py'. So the obligation checks (tracked path, selector, fixture, migration) are keyed on the presence of the `type` attribute, exactly the shape AUG-128 was filed to remove; AUG-128 fixed `method` for the block KIND check but not for obligation validation. Impact: the newly authored corpus (AUG-136) used method+path+selector without type, so EVERY test citation in specs/ was unverified by the tool — the corpus was green while a fabricated path would also be green. Coordinator worked around it by writing type=\"test\" on the 7 citation blocks; the product hole remains and the next author will hit it.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: obligation validation keys on `type=\"test\"` OR `method=\"test\"` (the AUG-128 rule), proven by a fixture pair that differs only in which attribute carries the word test: both are refused when their path does not exist, naming document + block + resolved path.\nPASS: the shipped corpus is validated without the type attribute workaround — i.e. a corpus written exactly as docs/XML-SPEC-SCHEMA.md describes is checked, or the doc requires type and a test asserts the doc's shape is the checked shape.\nPASS: a non-test method (manual/analysis/inspection) is still NOT forced through the test checks (no over-blocking), proven by a fixture.\nPASS: a regression test asserts that the corpus in specs/ has at least one block the validator refuses when its path is mutated, so the corpus cannot become decoration again.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:03:54.510509+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-11T02:02:35.42686+00:00", "foreman_note": "DISPATCHED SG9 (2026-11-06) as PROOF-ONLY scope. Driver re-measured the DEFECT IS FIXED at b93630b: copied specs/ to scratch, stripped every type=\"test\" (method=\"test\" runner+path+selector intact), mutated one path to tests/does-not-exist.py -> spec validate rc 2 'stale-test-ref: verification.xml: SPEC-OBL-CONSUMER-V1: tests/does-not-exist.py (resolved /home/kara/auger/tests/does-not-exist.py)', spec check identical rc 2; same corpus with correct paths rc 0 '3 document(s), 12 block(s), 7 reference(s) ok'. Residual assigned to the worker: the fixture PAIR differing only in which attribute carries test, the non-test-method no-over-blocking fixture, a regression test that mutates a citations path in a copy of the shipped specs/ and requires rc 2, and docs/XML-SPEC-SCHEMA.md reconciled to the measured either-attribute truth.\n\nSG9 LANDED 2026-11-06, awaiting a commit-bound GitReins verdict (debt AUG-154). Commit 7463dec on main (merge 5b0518c). Driver re-measured independently of the worker: a specs/ copy with one cited path mutated (spec-verbs.xml SPEC-VERBS-SELECTION-V1 -> tests/does-not-exist.py) refuses rc 2 stale-test-ref naming document+block+resolved path, and spec check returns the SAME refusal (verbs agree); unmutated copy rc 0 '3 document(s), 12 block(s), 7 reference(s) ok'. New proof file tests/test_spec_obligation_gate.py plus the fixture PAIR (type-only / method-only / neither) are named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm. Gate: worktree PASS 625 passed / 2 skipped 901.55s; merged main PASS 625 passed / 2 skipped 917.00s rc 0 (transcripts ~/.hermes/goals/sg9-wt-gate-r2.log, ~/.hermes/goals/sg9-main-gate.log).\n\nCLOSED on a commit-bound GitReins PASS. Task AUG-150 created with the row's four acceptance criteria as separate criteria (PROOF/FAILIF each); 'gitreins judge AUG-150' at HEAD 6009e742839e172daa465e9af09b30d77c6a220d (contains fix 7463dec, ancestor proven) -> pass_class=judged, tier1 PASS (secrets+lint+tests: full gate 722 passed / 2 skipped in 871.92s, GATE PASS, LIVE ARMS ran 2 skipped 0), tier2 COMPLETE 7/7 items PASS (4 authored + 3 derived), zero ungraded. Artifact .gitreins/history/2026-11-11/a9b1feeb/verdict.json (task_id=AUG-150, commit=6009e74); CLI printed 'Verdict saved: e2e3196b' but the directory is a9b1feeb, resolved by matching task_id AND commit. Driver re-measured the premise before dispatch: type-stripped specs/ copy with spec-verbs.xml path mutated to tests/does-not-exist.py refused rc 2 stale-test-ref by BOTH spec validate and spec check naming document+block+resolved path; shipped corpus validates ok; tests/test_spec_obligation_gate.py 12 passed in 1.82s, named in tests/gate.sh arm line 206.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worktree": "/home/kara/proj-wt-auger-xml-hardening", "branch": "wt/auger-xml-hardening", "commit_hash": "7463dec9f9009c6fe63bd8df413165ca1dc7ac57", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP"}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-151", "title": "docs/XML-SPEC-SCHEMA.md's worked example is invalid: it declares verifies on both sides, which the loader refuses as a reference cycle", "detail": {"fingerprint": "6a8249915983211a6a1d2066c34ca9d11d856b6227eca38b1c87b991809ed858"}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Found while authoring the corpus (AUG-136). The example shows a requirement with verifies=\"TEST\" AND the verification block with verifies=\"REQ\". The loader treats that mutual edge as `reference-cycle` (rc 2, reproduced on a scratch document) because the closure walk follows verifies in both directions. An author who copies the documented example gets a refusal with no hint that the documentation is the cause. Measured: one-directional edges (requirement owns verifies=verification) validate; the mutual shape is refused.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: docs/XML-SPEC-SCHEMA.md's example is a document that `auger spec validate` accepts, proven by a test that extracts the fenced example (or a copy of it) and validates it.\nPASS: the document states the edge rule in one sentence: verifies is declared on one side only (which side), and a mutual declaration is a cycle — with the refusal text quoted.\nPASS: if the loader is instead changed to accept the mutual shape (a defensible choice), the cycle detector's rule is updated and a test pins the new behaviour — but the doc and the code must agree either way.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:03:54.534751+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T21:03:54.534751+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": []}
