 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-154", "title": "Land commit-bound GitReins verdicts for the four landed-but-unjudged rows (AUG-127, AUG-123, AUG-135, AUG-120)", "detail": {"fingerprint": "253d5700b52e795cf47e13d0fc9bf569bf896ed1a146f8b0bb4aa7d2e4d5e3ea", "evidence": [{"run_id":"4343a720","ts":"2026-11-13T23:23:07.173438+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "MEASURED 2026-11-05 at main 909dbb0: four rows carry landed, gate-green, CI-green code and are STILL open for exactly one reason - no commit-bound GitReins verdict artifact exists for their trees. They are not code-complete work items any more; they are one bounded evidence action each. Leaving them open without this row makes every later driver tick re-verify finished work instead of advancing the plan.\nThe specific debt:\n- AUG-127 (SG3): implementation 12d2fe3, ancestor of origin/main, CI 42106886914 success, foreman_note records no verdict.\n- AUG-123 (SG3): code dae1769 on main, its 8 repository-root/obligation proofs green at HEAD (see evidence/auger-SG3/05-acceptance-runs.txt), blocked_reason (live JEV jev_already_answered=-1) reproduced ONCE at base and passed on immediate re-run plus two later full gates - a transient, not a standing block.\n- AUG-135 + AUG-120 (SG5): implementation c0e948f + 266d378, merged tip e1adcd3 (origin/main, parity 0/0), gate rc 0 twice (507 passed / 2 skipped in 859.62s worktree, 856.63s merged main), CI 42147268622 success. Rows hold guard=SKIP + commit=e1adcd3 + ci=GREEN and an explicit \"no verdict, none fabricated\" note.\nNone of these close without an artifact, and `boardctl update --status complete` refuses a non-resolving --evidence-run-id, so the debt cannot be paid by a note. It is one judge run per tree.\nCOST MEASURED, because it drives the plan: this repo's gitreins tier1 is `bash tests/gate.sh` with test_mode full and test_timeout 3600, and `evaluator.max_time` is 90m with a recorded history of tier-2 starving when the evaluator re-runs th